# Business Capability Ownership

**Status:** PRODUCT ARCHITECTURE GOVERNANCE · Frozen with ADR-019 (2026-07-25)  
**Applies to:** All future Product Architecture Reviews, Assessments, and ADRs  
**Related:** Pre-Launch Single Implementation Rule · ADR-019 §3A

## Principle

Every major business capability within Catalyst One shall have:

1. **One canonical business identity**  
2. **One canonical route**  
3. **One primary workspace**  
4. **One authoritative data owner**  
5. **One active implementation** (until official production Go-Live)

## Review expectation

Product Architecture Reviews must verify these five pillars for any new or replaced capability.

Replace programmes must also include **Legacy Retirement Impact** and conclude with **Replacement Certification**.

## Examples (certified identity)

| Capability | Identity | Route | Workspace | Data owner |
|------------|----------|-------|-----------|------------|
| Execution Hub | Loan Journey | `/loan-journey` | Execution Hub | Journey orchestration (not Deal/Opp SSOT) |
| Requirement capture | Lead Information | `/lead-information` | Lead Information | Opportunity Registry |
| Deal execution | Deal Workspace | `/deals/:dealId` (ADR-019) | Deal Workspace | Enterprise Deal Registry |

Loan File is **not** a business capability workspace after ADR-019 — it is an implementation/runtime artefact.
